WEBVTT

00:01.460 --> 00:07.132
(Fifth Year of Meiji)

00:07.216 --> 00:08.550
I really want it.

00:08.634 --> 00:09.885
It's not enough.

00:09.968 --> 00:12.054
I want more...

00:12.137 --> 00:13.514
Hurry.

00:14.306 --> 00:15.933
I really want it.

00:16.016 --> 00:17.601
I want it...

00:18.060 --> 00:20.646
The name Demon Capital
really lives up to its name.

00:21.813 --> 00:24.399
Demons are always on the prowl at night.

00:25.442 --> 00:27.486
If you don't mind me asking,

00:27.569 --> 00:29.154
what are your names?

01:02.104 --> 01:05.274
Maga... tsume.

01:15.367 --> 01:16.827
It's that name again.

01:17.703 --> 01:19.997
Excuse me, could it be...

01:20.497 --> 01:22.916
that you were the one who saved me?

01:23.584 --> 01:25.502
Kind of.

01:25.586 --> 01:26.837
I see.

01:26.920 --> 01:29.464
Thank you for saving me.

01:30.549 --> 01:33.677
Come to think of it,
I haven't introduced myself.

01:34.219 --> 01:36.346
My name is Himawari.

01:37.347 --> 01:38.640
That's a rare name.

01:38.724 --> 01:39.975
But it has a nice ring to it.

01:40.893 --> 01:45.314
Mother thought sunflowers suited me best,
so she gave me this name.

01:45.856 --> 01:47.900
I like it too.

01:47.983 --> 01:50.360
Please call me Himawari.

01:51.195 --> 01:54.823
But you're very polite.

01:54.907 --> 01:56.783
I turned eight this year.

01:56.867 --> 01:58.911
If I don't know any manners,

01:58.994 --> 02:01.163
I'll bring shame to Mother.

02:03.332 --> 02:05.292
What's wrong?

02:05.918 --> 02:07.085
Nothing.

02:07.753 --> 02:10.923
I have a daughter
who's a year older than you.

02:11.548 --> 02:14.051
That's why I'm a bit sentimental.

02:14.134 --> 02:16.303
If I may be so bold as to ask,

02:16.386 --> 02:17.638
how old are you?

02:17.721 --> 02:19.515
I'm turning 50 this year.

02:20.641 --> 02:22.226
You don't look it at all.

02:22.309 --> 02:23.727
I get that a lot.

02:24.228 --> 02:26.063
Did you come here alone?

02:26.480 --> 02:27.856
No.

02:27.940 --> 02:29.942
I came with Mother.

02:30.025 --> 02:31.652
But we got separated on the way.

02:31.735 --> 02:32.903
So you got lost.

02:32.986 --> 02:37.783
Mother probably thought
I had already gone home.

02:37.866 --> 02:40.452
If I can get to Nishioji,
I can go home by myself.

02:40.536 --> 02:42.788
Could I trouble you to walk me there?

02:43.247 --> 02:44.248
Sure.

02:49.837 --> 02:51.505
Let's go then,

02:51.839 --> 02:53.215
Uncle.

03:06.395 --> 03:11.733
(Sword of the Demon Hunter)

04:25.015 --> 04:29.018
(Demon Soba)

04:29.019 --> 04:33.890
(Demon Soba) (The Mitsuhashi Store)

04:38.153 --> 04:40.197
Good morning, Mr. Kadono.

04:42.741 --> 04:44.493
The weather is so nice.

04:44.576 --> 04:48.121
It would be great if I had more customers.

04:48.664 --> 04:50.916
It's only been open for a year.
Things can still grow from here.

04:50.999 --> 04:53.168
That would be great.

04:53.961 --> 04:57.047
(Demon Soba) (The Mitsuhashi Store)
Your shop has been open for five years, right?

04:57.130 --> 04:58.090
Yes.

04:58.173 --> 05:00.676
If I want to be acknowledged
by the people of Kyoto,

05:00.759 --> 05:03.428
it looks like it'll take a few years.

05:05.222 --> 05:06.056
Oh, right.

05:06.139 --> 05:09.268
I'll go to Demon Soba tonight.

05:09.351 --> 05:11.353
Thank you for your continued patronage.

05:40.424 --> 05:41.884
Nomari, it's time to wake up.

05:41.967 --> 05:42.968
Okay!

05:43.343 --> 05:45.470
Hey, you're already awake.

05:45.554 --> 05:48.599
You don't really need me
to come wake you up, do you?

05:48.682 --> 05:51.560
But I want you to wake me up, Father.

05:51.643 --> 05:53.854
Anyway, go wash your face first.

05:53.937 --> 05:55.063
Okay.

06:15.292 --> 06:16.752
Let's eat.

06:17.211 --> 06:18.879
Remember to chew well.

06:18.962 --> 06:20.297
I know.

06:24.468 --> 06:26.803
Were you okay yesterday?

06:26.887 --> 06:28.013
I wasn't hurt.

06:28.096 --> 06:29.431
No.

06:29.515 --> 06:31.266
That's not what I mean.

06:31.808 --> 06:34.811
Won't they arrest you
if they find out you're carrying a sword?

06:34.895 --> 06:37.105
As long as they don't find out,
I'll be fine.

06:37.940 --> 06:41.360
But you still have to be extra careful.

06:42.444 --> 06:45.113
I'll do my best, but it's not easy.

06:47.699 --> 06:50.536
There are more demons lately.

06:54.706 --> 06:56.375
Father...

06:59.962 --> 07:01.505
It'll be fine.

07:10.639 --> 07:11.640
Here's your lunch.

07:11.974 --> 07:13.517
Thank you.

07:13.600 --> 07:16.395
I'll be going now.

07:16.478 --> 07:17.563
Take care.

07:17.646 --> 07:18.647
Okay.

07:20.983 --> 07:23.318
Nanako, good morning.

07:23.402 --> 07:24.820
Good morning, Nomari.

07:24.903 --> 07:26.071
What should we do today?

07:26.154 --> 07:27.614
Let me think...

07:27.698 --> 07:30.242
I'm becoming more
and more of a family man.

07:36.874 --> 07:38.375
(Demon Soba)
Thank you for the food.

07:40.169 --> 07:41.795
Thank you for coming.

07:46.175 --> 07:47.634
You're not closed yet, right?

07:47.718 --> 07:50.888
No, I'm sorry. Today, we're already...

07:53.265 --> 07:54.808
Oh, it's you.

07:54.892 --> 07:58.812
You're so cold to your best friend.

07:58.896 --> 08:00.731
Since when am I your best friend?

08:00.814 --> 08:03.609
My, is it really okay for you to say that?

08:03.775 --> 08:06.695
Back then,
when you wanted to build this shop,

08:06.778 --> 08:09.072
who was it that helped you find the land

08:09.156 --> 08:11.033
and handle all the paperwork?

08:11.533 --> 08:14.286
Mr. Jinya Kadono, who was it again?

08:16.914 --> 08:18.373
Kadono...

08:18.457 --> 08:20.375
Jinya Kadono.

08:22.544 --> 08:26.173
This surname doesn't roll off my tongue.

08:26.840 --> 08:28.175
Can I just call you Jinya?

08:28.258 --> 08:29.718
Do as you please.

08:29.801 --> 08:32.387
Well then, Jinya, I'll have kitsune soba.

08:32.471 --> 08:34.765
Heikichi, you can have the same, right?

08:43.899 --> 08:45.025
Master.

08:45.108 --> 08:47.444
Can't we eat somewhere else?

08:47.528 --> 08:49.530
Why must we have dinner
at a demon's restaurant?

08:49.613 --> 08:52.407
Hey, watch what you say.

08:52.491 --> 08:55.369
Thankfully, there are no other customers.

08:56.411 --> 08:58.956
Of course I know that much.

08:59.039 --> 09:01.625
But aren't we supposed
to stand against demons?

09:04.253 --> 09:05.337
A demon is the refuge

09:05.420 --> 09:07.881
where human obsessions sink
at the end of their path.

09:07.965 --> 09:11.009
Whether we should act or not,
we must first tell right from wrong.

09:11.385 --> 09:13.971
Is that out of pride
as a tsukumogami user?

09:14.429 --> 09:17.391
It's out of basic courtesy as a human.

09:17.474 --> 09:20.435
Since we can turn emotions into power,

09:20.519 --> 09:24.273
we must value feelings
more than anyone else.

09:27.276 --> 09:29.361
It's really not easy being a master.

09:30.571 --> 09:31.989
I know, right?

09:32.990 --> 09:35.200
She should be here soon.

09:41.915 --> 09:43.625
She's the client.

09:49.339 --> 09:50.257
Nomari.

09:50.340 --> 09:52.259
Yes, I'll wait inside.

09:54.678 --> 09:57.723
I've explained your background to her.

09:57.806 --> 10:01.101
Her master and I are old acquaintances.

10:01.810 --> 10:03.854
I'll leave the rest to you.

10:07.399 --> 10:09.943
I'm Jinya Kadono.

10:10.027 --> 10:12.237
I slay demons for a living.

10:12.946 --> 10:14.615
Your name is...

10:15.157 --> 10:18.368
You can call me Kaneomi for now.

10:20.787 --> 10:22.831
A work by the late
Sengoku-period swordsmith,

10:22.915 --> 10:24.666
Kaneomi.

10:24.750 --> 10:26.835
Yatonomori Kaneomi.

10:27.127 --> 10:28.754
So you know.

10:29.671 --> 10:31.715
Please tell me the details.

10:32.633 --> 10:34.801
On the bridge over the Kamo River...

10:34.885 --> 10:38.847
Every night,
a demon appears on Gojo Bridge.

10:38.931 --> 10:40.807
Her name is Jishibari.

10:40.891 --> 10:43.310
I'd like you to capture her.

10:43.393 --> 10:44.811
Capture her?

10:44.895 --> 10:45.896
Yes.

10:45.979 --> 10:49.691
That demon took away
something most precious to me.

10:50.442 --> 10:52.194
I want to get it back.

10:53.320 --> 10:56.990
I've already lost to Jishibari once.

10:57.449 --> 11:00.744
That's why I'm asking you, Lord Kadono,

11:00.827 --> 11:04.081
who can slay demons
with just one sword, for help.

11:04.498 --> 11:06.041
You want revenge...

11:06.875 --> 11:09.253
Would you like me
to explain the whole story?

11:09.628 --> 11:12.130
If you don't want to say it,
don't push yourself.

11:12.214 --> 11:14.508
Thank you for understanding.

11:16.969 --> 11:21.974
Well then, please accept this deposit
of 60 yen for the commission.

11:26.395 --> 11:30.774
Actually, that demon named Jishibari
looks exactly like me.

11:30.858 --> 11:31.692
Huh?

11:32.276 --> 11:34.611
Have you heard of "Futari Shizuka"?

11:35.279 --> 11:36.446
Yes, I have.

11:36.530 --> 11:39.950
It's a kind of white flower that grows
in secluded mountain fields, right?

11:40.033 --> 11:42.578
It's very similar to a flower
called "Hitori Shizuka."

11:42.661 --> 11:44.705
But it's said that
it's called "Futari Shizuka"

11:44.788 --> 11:47.749
because it has two spikes.

11:49.543 --> 11:52.421
Lord Kadono, you know a lot about flowers.

11:52.504 --> 11:56.466
But the Futari Shizuka I meant
is Zeami's Noh play.

11:59.011 --> 12:00.762
At Katte Shrine in Yoshino,

12:00.846 --> 12:04.349
a woman went to gather wild greens
as an offering to the gods.

12:04.433 --> 12:06.810
She ended up being possessed
by the spirit of Shizuka Gozen

12:06.894 --> 12:10.230
and ultimately danced
in front of the Shinto priest.

12:11.899 --> 12:14.902
Because the woman
was possessed by Shizuka Gozen,

12:14.985 --> 12:17.863
she was able to perform her dance.

12:18.530 --> 12:20.407
But in the middle of the dance,

12:20.490 --> 12:23.827
the spirit of Shizuka Gozen
appeared behind her.

12:25.329 --> 12:29.208
The possessed woman
and the spirit of Shizuka Gozen.

12:29.291 --> 12:31.168
That's why it's called
"Futari Shizuka", Two Shizukas.

12:31.251 --> 12:32.252
Yes.

12:32.336 --> 12:35.631
Reasonably, the woman should have been
released from the possession by then.

12:35.714 --> 12:37.966
But she continued to dance.

12:38.967 --> 12:41.595
What is it that drives the woman
to continue dancing?

12:42.346 --> 12:44.056
Unfortunately, my knowledge is shallow.

12:44.139 --> 12:46.350
I can't make sense
of such a complicated topic.

12:46.850 --> 12:48.143
Besides...

12:49.686 --> 12:52.898
it seems like it's time for me
to meet Shizuka Gozen.

12:59.571 --> 13:01.823
Today, I'm going to take it back for sure.

13:02.282 --> 13:03.700
Oh, my...

13:03.784 --> 13:06.828
Still like doing pointless things, I see.

13:06.912 --> 13:08.455
You brought a man with you today?

13:09.206 --> 13:10.541
I'm Jinya.

13:10.624 --> 13:12.793
So you're Jinya.

13:12.876 --> 13:15.254
I've heard rumors about you.

13:15.337 --> 13:16.880
I'm Jishibari,

13:16.964 --> 13:21.051
currently hunting humans
under the orders of Lady Magatsume.

13:21.552 --> 13:22.761
The Magatsume you mentioned,

13:22.845 --> 13:24.304
is she your master?

13:24.763 --> 13:27.015
No, she's not.

13:27.099 --> 13:30.227
- Then--
- Did you come here just to talk to me?

13:30.519 --> 13:31.937
You're right.

13:32.020 --> 13:35.107
We'll talk about the rest
after I defeat you.

13:35.190 --> 13:36.275
Lord Kadono,

13:36.358 --> 13:38.485
that demon is no ordinary demon.

13:38.569 --> 13:40.654
Please be careful,
and don't lower your guard.

13:40.737 --> 13:42.239
Thank you for the warning.

13:46.869 --> 13:48.036
Chains?

13:52.291 --> 13:54.543
My name is Jishibari.

13:55.335 --> 13:57.254
And my ability is also called...

13:57.337 --> 13:58.755
"Jishibari."

14:11.810 --> 14:12.936
Oh, wow.

14:13.020 --> 14:16.023
Don't tell me you have eyes
on the back of your head too?

14:16.732 --> 14:17.774
Dash.

14:21.820 --> 14:24.448
This really is a little dangerous.

14:26.408 --> 14:27.409
Flying Blade.

14:41.590 --> 14:44.092
So you're a demon.

14:46.053 --> 14:48.472
All right, let's continue.

14:49.097 --> 14:51.141
Hello, Uncle.

14:56.855 --> 14:58.273
You're...

14:58.357 --> 15:00.943
Thank you for saving me last night.

15:01.818 --> 15:03.445
You're very skilled indeed.

15:03.529 --> 15:06.740
You were able to push my younger sister this far.

15:06.823 --> 15:08.867
I really didn't expect that.

15:09.326 --> 15:10.536
She's your younger sister?

15:10.911 --> 15:13.664
Jishibari is my younger sister.

15:13.747 --> 15:15.707
It might be hard to tell,

15:15.791 --> 15:18.252
but I'm the eldest daughter.

15:20.003 --> 15:21.630
I see.

15:21.713 --> 15:26.260
So the demons that surrounded you
last night weren't trying to attack you.

15:27.052 --> 15:28.303
That's right.

15:28.387 --> 15:31.473
Mother entrusted those children to me.

15:31.557 --> 15:32.766
But you know what?

15:32.850 --> 15:34.393
Even if it was a misunderstanding,

15:34.476 --> 15:38.272
you reached out to help me out of concern.

15:38.355 --> 15:40.732
That makes me very happy.

15:44.444 --> 15:46.822
I don't think I've told you this before.

15:46.905 --> 15:50.284
My mother's name is Magatsume.

15:50.659 --> 15:51.910
Sister...

15:52.661 --> 15:53.829
To be honest,

15:53.912 --> 15:56.790
I'm not confident
that I can take that man down.

15:56.874 --> 15:58.292
In that case...

16:00.335 --> 16:01.753
I see.

16:01.837 --> 16:03.380
That's a good idea.

16:04.506 --> 16:05.841
Uncle,

16:05.924 --> 16:08.719
my sister and I will team up
and fight from now on.

16:08.802 --> 16:10.387
You won't mind, right?

16:10.470 --> 16:11.889
Do whatever you want.

16:12.306 --> 16:14.391
Let's get started then.

16:29.448 --> 16:30.282
Now.

16:30.365 --> 16:31.200
Okay.

16:37.247 --> 16:38.248
Dash.

16:43.670 --> 16:45.172
Lord Kadono!

16:47.674 --> 16:49.259
That's right.

16:49.343 --> 16:53.263
How could Uncle ignore someone
who's about to get hurt

16:53.347 --> 16:55.557
right in front of him?

17:02.105 --> 17:03.774
I got you.

17:08.695 --> 17:09.947
What did you do?

17:10.030 --> 17:11.406
Care to guess?

17:14.701 --> 17:15.827
Dash.

17:17.079 --> 17:19.540
I've already sealed your speed.

17:22.209 --> 17:23.126
Ms. Kaneomi,

17:23.210 --> 17:24.378
run!

17:25.462 --> 17:26.505
I can't.

17:26.588 --> 17:28.382
My leg can't move at all.

17:32.928 --> 17:35.055
Flying Blade is pretty troublesome too.

17:35.138 --> 17:36.890
I'll seal it while I'm at it.

17:45.274 --> 17:47.526
Sorry, I only ended up dragging you down.

17:47.609 --> 17:48.610
Don't say that.

17:49.862 --> 17:54.157
So one chain can seal one ability.

17:54.241 --> 17:55.325
That's right.

17:55.409 --> 17:58.036
Now you have no chance of winning.

18:01.206 --> 18:02.249
What's that supposed to mean?

18:02.332 --> 18:04.168
You really are an idiot.

18:04.376 --> 18:05.669
What did you say?

18:08.839 --> 18:09.715
Don't!

18:11.925 --> 18:13.051
Invisibility.

18:17.556 --> 18:19.016
He's right in front of you!

18:25.731 --> 18:26.815
Damn it...

18:26.899 --> 18:28.525
Let's retreat for now.

18:31.320 --> 18:32.362
But--

18:32.446 --> 18:36.074
You haven't fulfilled Mother's orders yet.

18:36.158 --> 18:38.660
I won't allow you to die here.

18:39.745 --> 18:42.831
I... I understand.

18:45.334 --> 18:46.793
Well then, Uncle.

18:46.877 --> 18:48.504
I'm really sorry.

18:48.587 --> 18:50.631
Please allow us to take our leave first.

18:50.797 --> 18:52.633
I'm sorry, but I won't let you go.

18:52.716 --> 18:53.717
Behind you!

19:13.612 --> 19:15.030
Lord Kadono.

19:17.741 --> 19:20.619
Was that the thing
that bound you just now?

19:21.620 --> 19:23.080
I'm sorry.

19:23.330 --> 19:25.082
Don't worry about it.

19:25.165 --> 19:27.084
It was my mistake.

19:28.418 --> 19:30.003
Magatsume...

19:33.757 --> 19:36.927
Nothing goes my way.

19:44.518 --> 19:45.519
(Demon Soba)

19:45.602 --> 19:47.145
Thank you for coming.

19:49.481 --> 19:50.899
Thank you for the food.

19:54.778 --> 19:56.697
I'm back.

19:58.073 --> 19:58.991
Welcome home.

19:59.074 --> 20:00.534
How was school today?

20:01.243 --> 20:04.413
We had arithmetic and calligraphy today.

20:04.496 --> 20:07.124
I'll learn quickly
so I can help out at the shop soon.

20:09.293 --> 20:11.253
I'm almost done here.

20:11.336 --> 20:12.838
Shall we have some tea together?

20:12.921 --> 20:14.339
Can I?

20:15.507 --> 20:18.343
I'll have the kakiage soba next.

20:18.635 --> 20:20.095
Hmm?

20:20.470 --> 20:22.848
Hey, that's already the third bowl.

20:23.182 --> 20:25.559
I didn't shortchange you, did I?

20:25.642 --> 20:27.853
Even if you did pay,
you've eaten way too much.

20:27.936 --> 20:30.647
Besides, why are you still staying here?

20:30.981 --> 20:33.609
If you're planning
to continue pursuing Jishibari,

20:33.692 --> 20:36.403
I'd like to stay here for the time being.

20:36.737 --> 20:41.283
Who knows, maybe one day
they'll come knocking on their own.

20:42.701 --> 20:46.246
A young woman moving
into a man's house just like that.

20:46.330 --> 20:48.540
How could such a thing ever be allowed?

20:48.624 --> 20:50.626
Since I've already paid the deposit,

20:50.709 --> 20:52.503
I'm the client.

20:52.586 --> 20:55.255
And you know very clearly
what happened last night...

20:56.006 --> 20:58.884
Can't you make an exception for me?

21:02.679 --> 21:04.223
What do you think?

21:06.850 --> 21:09.561
Father, what's going on?

21:13.190 --> 21:15.234
You ordered kakiage soba, right?

21:15.317 --> 21:17.402
I'll take that as a yes.

21:17.486 --> 21:18.487
What?

21:22.324 --> 21:26.245
I'll be in your care from now on.

21:27.496 --> 21:29.122
Please make my soba a large portion.

21:35.212 --> 21:36.213
What?

21:36.505 --> 21:37.673
Father.

21:37.756 --> 21:39.675
What exactly is going on?

21:50.853 --> 21:54.147
That girl is very close to Uncle.

21:54.231 --> 21:55.649
Huh? What?

21:55.732 --> 21:57.192
What did you see?

21:57.276 --> 22:00.279
I feel so frustrated,

22:00.362 --> 22:01.697
Mother.
